{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/998945-how-do-people-use-the-strix","id":998945,"title":"How do people use the Strix?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-05T16:47:32-07:00","id":998945,"title":"How do people use the Strix?","content":"I had this vague plan for my Seattle game of looking up hauntings and urban legends and basing a strix or two on that, but Seattle doesn't seem to have a lot of urban legends that'd work.<br /> <br /> So I think I'll create an urban legend and it'll be about a strix. Hopefully some of the Seattle hauntings might be of use (and there are <i>so many</i>).<br /> <br /> But mostly I'm wondering how people use strix? How many might be in a given area? I don't want to make them a central thing, but more a somewhat spooky thing that eventually comes to a head, but isn't the central conflict (what that is will depend on the players).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T18:17:32-07:00","id":998970,"title":"","content":"I think you're on the right track. I think the Strix work best as boogeymen, so I hint at them often but actually bring them in quite sparingly. As for how many might be in an area, I would say that depends on what's happening (or about to happen) in the area. Strix can sense impending disasters and are drawn to them, so you can use them like black dogs (or what ever doom omen you like). A glimpse of an avian shape out of the corner of the eye can herald a coming battle. A small handful in a domain can mean the whole city is at risk. Larger numbers could foreshadow major story climaxes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T19:42:15-07:00","id":999005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/998945-how-do-people-use-the-strix?p=998970#post998970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you're on the right track. I think the Strix work best as boogeymen, so I hint at them often but actually bring them in quite sparingly. As for how many might be in an area, I would say that depends on what's happening (or about to happen) in the area. Strix can sense impending disasters and are drawn to them, so you can use them like black dogs (or what ever doom omen you like). A glimpse of an avian shape out of the corner of the eye can herald a coming battle. A small handful in a domain can mean the whole city is at risk. Larger numbers could foreshadow major story climaxes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, that does help. It didn't seem like the best way to use them was as targets to DPS down.<br /> <br /> Now to draft a complaint to the State of Washington about the lack of decent urban legends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T20:22:13-07:00","id":999032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/998945-how-do-people-use-the-strix?p=998970#post998970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so you can use them like black dogs (or what ever doom omen you like).</div> </div> </div> </div>I had a DM who uses them exactly like that....sorta. One of the players made a character, put all his dot in occultism with a specialization on Strix because well new name of the game (at the time), and was incredible paranoic IC and OOC about them. One thing led to another and he became prince, i think we were playing the continuation of the demo (i enter the campaign late), so every time he was gonna take certain descisions a shadowy owlish figure would appear as an ill omen and he would change his mind.<br /> <br /> Which in reality was another player who used a discipline (i think he was a mekhet, again it was a while ago) to manipulate the player to the descisions he wanted by passing secret texts to the DM.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T00:04:00-07:00","id":999096,"title":"","content":"Honestly, my favorite part about using the strix is in how I use the rumors of Strix. Nothing stirs up more trouble than a supposed strix sighting, and you have people left and right accusing political rivals of strixdom, and the whole city is a mess; and in comes the strix who only needs to pull a few strings to set the city in flames.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T03:39:58-08:00","id":999142,"title":"","content":"I am using a trapped strix as a MacGuffin in Portland, with the rumor that the Carthian law is what keeps it trapped. Uncork that figurative bottle and you'd have a horrible purging of carthian vampires and a power vacuum to fill according to Invictus rumors, or maybe <u>all</u> vampires would meet Final Death the result. It is my &quot;setting cleanser&quot; which is available in game should PCs figure it out what the innuendo and tainted rumors surrounding the founding of the current political system, or plot driven circumstance could cause it to, should the setting need a vampire shake up. The strix as designed can descretely wipe out the whole kindred community in the city and besides fleeing there ia little that can be done to stop it. <br /> <br /> I also allow templates to have Mystery Cult Initiation, and have a few competing Mystery Cults centered around worshipping a powerful Strix in Seattle, which has lesser strix act as resentful servants for the 5 dot members of the mystery cult.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 11-06-2016, 06:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T06:39:17-08:00","id":999191,"title":"","content":"I use a highly houseruled setting and I do not use Strix as they are described in the official setting. However, I use one version of them, and I think I can relate to your question a bit. I don't use Strix as separate entities because I would rather have Vampires as main antagonists, and older, weirder vampires as boogeymen. I prefer to have vampires be the pinacle of horror and I don't really need something else to top it.<br /> <br /> In my homebrew setting, when a vampire is destroyed, her dark essence, the Curse itself that makes her a vampire, is free to leave the body. This dark essence is the &quot;supernatural DNA&quot; of the vampire, as well as her consciousness. Basically, it's everything except the body. The higher their Blood POtency at the moment of their death, the less time their dark essence takes to reform and become strong enough to possess a body, allowing the vampire to be reborn. This dark essence freed from the body IS the Strix. They can possess humans or vampires (at higher risk but greater reward) to be reborn and often seek the ones responsible for their death in order to possess them. <br /> <br /> This is the reason why destroying vampires is not well regarded. They can come back and there is virtually no way to prevent a possession although it is resolved woth a clash of will. As a result, I use Strix,or at least, my equivalent of them, as a potential threat to vampires who destroy one of their kind. It also gives vampires a reason to use stakes and keep their torpid ennemies hidden instead of destroying them. The only way to cause final death is through Diablerie, the Strix or Dark essence being completely consumed. <br /> <br /> When a Shadow is sighted, vampires know one of their kind is about to rise again, and that any of them could be potentially used as a vessel. Thus, despite the difference of setting, I tend to use them a lot like some of the people who answered you, that is, as a potential threat hanging over the kindred's heads and influencing their society as a whole rather than as direct antagonists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12610-lestat","name":"Lestat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12610_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T07:31:56-08:00","id":999206,"title":"","content":"I have strix-tainted ghosts around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T07:43:30-08:00","id":999209,"title":"","content":"I have been using the Strix as more of Omens of Bad Shit Coming, than using them as the threat itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T06:09:24-08:00","id":999696,"title":"","content":"I ran <b>Blood and Smoke</b> before it was retitled, so I wanted to make the Strix prominent, but I still kept them as a mysterious threat striking from the shadows, probing for weaknesses and turning the city's Kindred on each other. The players' characters tried to find a way to repel them, and their best bet was reviving an elder in torpor who none of the local vampires wanted to come back - saving the city at a cost of setting off a Kindred civil war. Even defeating the Strix was cause for a violent upheaval.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T06:28:02-08:00","id":999705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The players' characters tried to find a way to repel them, and their best bet was reviving an elder in torpor who none of the local vampires wanted to come back - saving the city at a cost of setting off a Kindred civil war. Even defeating the Strix was cause for a violent upheaval. </div> </div> </div>Great idea. I love games of consequences, whatever the choices that are made. Perfect example of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12610-lestat","name":"Lestat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12610_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T09:17:00-08:00","id":999781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/998945-how-do-people-use-the-strix?p=999005#post999005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now to draft a complaint to the State of Washington about the lack of decent urban legends.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, we do have one of the Big ones: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bigfoot\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bigfoot</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T11:28:31-08:00","id":999832,"title":"","content":"I've only used the Strix in one chronicle so far (and it was Mage) but I used them has independent agents who came because of impending disaster and worked to prevent anyone from stopping it.<br /> \u200bRegarding a lack of urban legends, don't get caught up on them being urban. The Strix, even individuals, can hang around for centuries, so don't neglect older legends that predate the white man's arrival.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T12:21:00-08:00","id":999862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/998945-how-do-people-use-the-strix?p=999781#post999781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, we do have one of the Big ones: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bigfoot\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bigfoot</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly the kind that doesn't really work for what I want, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T12:21:42-08:00","id":999864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/998945-how-do-people-use-the-strix?p=999832#post999832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've only used the Strix in one chronicle so far (and it was Mage) but I used them has independent agents who came because of impending disaster and worked to prevent anyone from stopping it.<br /> \u200bRegarding a lack of urban legends, don't get caught up on them being urban. The Strix, even individuals, can hang around for centuries, so don't neglect older legends that predate the white man's arrival.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am looking at more than just modern urban legends. I was just disappointed in the urban legends present in modern Washington.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T12:32:37-08:00","id":999882,"title":"","content":"Thanks for this. I've honestly left them out of my games for a while, because I'm not sure how to incorporate them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>International Relations Scholar, Salesman, and GM. Guess which one of those is my favorite?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12305-obrimosmaintenance","name":"ObrimosMaintenance","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T00:21:16-08:00","id":1000174,"title":"","content":"So I had a longer reply written out but my browser did something I still don't understand and reloaded the previous page, erasing my entire message. I can't really reconstruct everything I said, so I'll just say thanks to everyone for their takes. I really appreciate the idea of strix as being bad omens and I'm almost certainly going to go that route for my game.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T04:47:22-08:00","id":1000219,"title":"","content":"One of my players turned a failure on a feeding roll into a dramatic failure last session, looking for guidance the core suggested the idea they attempted to feed from a Strix. Had the Strix turn the tables and drain some his essence without him noticing. Later he saw her out again at a party, correctly surmising the weird girl was why he woke up starving. Told her off, lashed out with his aura and she left the party they were at. Then when he went home to sleep there was the girl's dead body.<br /> <br /> I think I'll leave it there. He doesn't know what she was, what really happened, and now he's got a corpse to deal with that he's been seen in public with on several occasions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T07:31:54-08:00","id":1000264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/998945-how-do-people-use-the-strix?p=999862#post999862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Exactly the kind that doesn't really work for what I want, though.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh yeah, I realize that old Squatch doesn't ring Strix at all. Just defending my home <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But, yeah, there isn't a lot of urban legends around here that I can think of to help really. As someone else said though, you can use the First Nation's peoples mythology as a good source.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T10:54:36-08:00","id":1000331,"title":"","content":"I feel like the thing is...<br /> <br /> Strix are to Vampires ehat Vampires are to everything else.<br /> <br /> Has no one used them to control NPCs or PCs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T17:01:28-08:00","id":1003682,"title":"","content":"I've just started running a V:tM 2e campaign set in London, with the Strix forming a major part of the backstory. Having read the hints about London in &quot;Shadows of the UK&quot; for Werewolf the Forsaken 1e, I found myself looking at the hints about &quot;The Cull&quot;- how every few centuries, all but a handful of the vampires in London would be destroyed by some unknown agency and that the estimated time for the next Cull was coming up. With the 1e stuff being about a decade old, I decided to create a chronicle set in the aftermath of the Cull. And after reading Requiem for Rome and Fall of the Camarilla, the Strix were an obvious choice for what could wipe a city clean of Kindred.<br /> <br /> So- one of the largest and richest cities in the world is currently utterly devoid of any vampiric presence. A prize ripe for the taking.<br /> <br /> The players were created by the Ordo Dracul using the &quot;Mass Embrace&quot; Scale, as part of a move by some Elders of the Covenant to get the increased numbers they'd need to capture as many of the city's sites of occult significance as possible. Unfortunately the Dragons had moved too soon- the danger wasn't over, and they perished along with most of the newly created vampires. The PCs were the only survivors, barely escaping the burning haven and fleeing into the city.<br /> <br /> Now they're alone in London, with no other vampires to inform them of how their powers work and no vampire society, for good or ill. There are strange and terrible rumours of Owls all across the city, many of the movers-and-shakers of the human world in London are acting erratically or becoming ill (Ghouls and mind-influenced puppets with masters gone) leading to an increase in chaos, and all manner of strange events being whispered about online or even on the mainstream media (the usual level of supernatural activity for London, but now the ones who used to cover it up are gone). They have an opportunity to seize great power and influence- but then they'll have to struggle to keep it, because eventually more vampires will come to London to try and claim the empty capital as their own.<br /> <br /> And there are glimpses of shadowy Owls and the letters &quot;VII&quot; being daubed in blood across the city...<br /> <br /> Most players haven't played WoD before, or have only played the OWod Vampire: the Masquerade. Only one has read the 2e books, and he's managing to keep quiet and do a reasonable job of playing his character as ignorant, so the Strix are making for a very good mystery hanging over the setting (as is VII and how they relate to them). Thus far hints got limited to an OOC exchange.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Owls are not what they seem!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Not what they seem? You don't know the half of it...&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12331-tantavalist","name":"Tantavalist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T18:51:49-08:00","id":1003734,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12331-tantavalist\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12331\" data-vbnamecard=\"12331\">Tantavalist</a> That is really cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T00:41:31-08:00","id":1008449,"title":"","content":"In my fictional city, the Strix waged a war some centuries prior to the modern nights. While they were seemingly all wiped out or driven off (with some help from, among other things, the local Native American werewolf packs), many of the city's current customs reflect the fear of their return. Owls were secretly rendered extinct and any sightings of owls within city limits must be reported immediately. They're not permitted for use as symbolism, and vampires who develop too much of a fascination with the deepest shadows are closely watched. Certain blood rituals and even some city development is targeted at making sure <i>they </i>cannot come back again.<br /> <br /> Will it work? Not likely, but before ever showing a Strix, I would just as soon tell of the resurgence of owls in the area, or strange occurrences that <i>could </i>be Strix-related, but only the real scholars would know, and there's no proof. Only shadows in the corners of your eyes....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}